INTENTIONAL DEVIATION FROM UPSTREAM: architect decision D3 (PR #4).

Not oracle output. A Gitea-style modified file whose head-content fetch
failed (head_status fetch_failed, no head.txt) while its patch, taken from
the PR's .diff, is present and trustworthy.

review-mcp renders the patch normally in every view, unextended because the
head content is nil (spec section 3.2). It never shows the unreadable notice,
which would claim that no diff is available. The notice is reserved for
head_status fetch_failed with an empty patch (oracle case
testdata/upstream/unreadable).

Upstream PR-Agent at 8e5a929 would extend this patch against an empty head
string, so it cannot produce these outputs. They were derived by running the
upstream oracle (gen_goldens.py) on a twin case: same path, type and patch,
head_status "full", no base.txt and no head.txt. Upstream then leaves the patch
unextended (no original file) and renders it normally. See
testdata/upstream/README.md, section "Deviations".
